res first-term Republican Michael Baumgartner in a rematch against Democrat Carmela Conroy, whom he defeated in 2024. The seat leans Republican by about five points, and Baumgartner enters with a decisive financial advantage, having raised roughly four times as much as Conroy and holding a large cash edge. Conroy has modest resources and little outside support on either side.\n\nExpert raters mostly call the district Safe Republican, with a few at Likely Republican, and prediction markets give Baumgartner about an 81 percent chance of winning. The only recent poll, from May and sponsored by a Democratic-leaning firm, showed a closer 53-47 contest, but it predates the general election. The forecast expects Baumgartner to win by roughly nine points, with meaningful but limited uncertainty.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0968, "margin": -8.12}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.1087, "margin": -9.0}]}